1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:29,980
Thank you so much for joining us.

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:59,980
Thank you so much for joining us.

3
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:04,980
We have an internal debate in staff of what's going to be the more popular of the two services.

4
00:01:04,980 --> 00:01:10,700
It seems like the morning people are, you guys are awesome.

5
00:01:10,700 --> 00:01:14,120
We don't, you know, I don't encourage gambling,

6
00:01:14,120 --> 00:01:19,600
but our new executive pastor did send an email to our staff asking for them to guess

7
00:01:19,600 --> 00:01:21,200
how many people are going to be at each service.

8
00:01:21,280 --> 00:01:24,440
And he did offer for me to buy the winner lunch.

9
00:01:24,440 --> 00:01:27,120
So I'm like passively gambling.

10
00:01:27,120 --> 00:01:32,520
And, you know, apparently that's what we're doing here at Canvas Community Church.

11
00:01:32,880 --> 00:01:37,200
If you are new or newer here, we do say we are a church full of real people

12
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:41,720
with real lives learning to follow Jesus in a difficult cultural moment.

13
00:01:41,720 --> 00:01:46,740
And we would say that Easter and the resurrection of Jesus is at the center of everything for us.

14
00:01:46,740 --> 00:01:49,340
This is the biggest day of the year.

15
00:01:49,340 --> 00:01:52,720
But in reality, it's something that we celebrate every week.

16
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:59,140
The reason that we meet together on Sunday mornings is because that marks the day that Jesus rose from the dead.

17
00:01:59,140 --> 00:02:00,680
It marks the day of new creation.

18
00:02:00,680 --> 00:02:06,120
And I've been thinking a lot about how to explain that in the most simplest of terms

19
00:02:06,120 --> 00:02:08,480
now that I have a three-year-old asking me questions.

20
00:02:09,520 --> 00:02:15,220
How do you explain that the garden is being restored, that new creation is here and present

21
00:02:15,220 --> 00:02:19,280
now that Jesus has crushed the head of the serpent when there is still darkness?

22
00:02:19,280 --> 00:02:24,900
Like Amy prayed, many of you are coming into this place with difficulty and pain,

23
00:02:24,900 --> 00:02:27,920
and we are singing celebratory songs about the resurrection.

24
00:02:27,920 --> 00:02:30,760
And yet for you, you have not yet experienced the resurrection.

25
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:37,820
And as I drove here this morning for the sunrise service, for those really morning people,

26
00:02:37,820 --> 00:02:43,960
I just, I watched the sun kind of coming over the mountains on the way from my house,

27
00:02:43,960 --> 00:02:45,300
and I just saw a light spreading.

28
00:02:45,300 --> 00:02:48,840
And yet I looked towards the sunrise, and I saw a light spreading,

29
00:02:48,840 --> 00:02:52,800
and I looked in the opposite direction, and there was still darkness in many places.

30
00:02:52,800 --> 00:02:57,560
I think that's such a helpful way for us to think about new creation dawning

31
00:02:57,560 --> 00:03:03,840
and Christ crushing the head of the serpent and life of the garden spreading.

32
00:03:03,840 --> 00:03:06,380
It is spreading, and it will continue to spread.

33
00:03:06,380 --> 00:03:09,400
And one day the Scripture says that we will no longer need the sun

34
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:12,520
because the presence of the Lord will be our light.

35
00:03:12,520 --> 00:03:16,680
But until that day comes, many of you in here are in the shadows.

36
00:03:16,680 --> 00:03:21,400
You are experiencing darkness, and I do not want that to go unseen.

37
00:03:21,920 --> 00:03:28,660
And I do not want you to hear a trite message where we just ignore the pain and brokenness of this world

38
00:03:28,660 --> 00:03:29,660
because we do not.

39
00:03:29,660 --> 00:03:33,240
But we do not grieve as people without hope.

40
00:03:33,240 --> 00:03:38,440
So I hope to communicate that more in full with the rest of my time this morning.

41
00:03:38,440 --> 00:03:41,080
Let's go ahead and pray for our time.

42
00:03:41,080 --> 00:03:44,220
Father in heaven, you are so good.

43
00:03:46,500 --> 00:03:54,880
We thank you for the reality of a garden being renewed through the faithful one, Jesus Christ.

44
00:03:54,880 --> 00:04:01,500
And God, we sometimes experience resurrection life

45
00:04:01,500 --> 00:04:06,420
and sometimes experience the chaos and destruction of life outside the garden.

46
00:04:06,420 --> 00:04:11,560
And yet we know in the midst of both of those experiences,

47
00:04:11,560 --> 00:04:14,440
you are present, you are faithful, and that you love us.

48
00:04:16,360 --> 00:04:21,420
Sin broke a lot of things and messed a lot of things up,

49
00:04:21,420 --> 00:04:24,380
but what it never interrupted was your love for us.

50
00:04:24,380 --> 00:04:29,700
Even as you are in tears placing Adam and Eve outside of the garden,

51
00:04:29,700 --> 00:04:32,800
you clothe them and you promise to send them a savior.

52
00:04:32,800 --> 00:04:36,460
Your love has never run out and it never will run out.

53
00:04:36,460 --> 00:04:38,500
And if we're in here and we do not yet feel that,

54
00:04:38,500 --> 00:04:41,100
we have not yet experienced that, I pray that we would.

55
00:04:41,100 --> 00:04:44,580
And God, for those of us who have experienced it

56
00:04:44,580 --> 00:04:50,140
and yet are doubting it or struggling or wrestling with whether it's true,

57
00:04:50,140 --> 00:04:51,960
God, give us renewed hope.

58
00:04:51,960 --> 00:04:55,520
In Jesus' name I pray, amen.

59
00:04:55,520 --> 00:04:58,880
We're gonna start with a little bit of crowd participation.

60
00:04:58,880 --> 00:05:01,220
Before we get to the main part,

61
00:05:01,220 --> 00:05:02,640
just so that we know either

62
00:05:02,640 --> 00:05:06,480
our older generation in the room

63
00:05:06,480 --> 00:05:08,120
or the holiest people in the room,

64
00:05:08,120 --> 00:05:11,080
raise your hand if you never had a video game console in your house.

65
00:05:12,960 --> 00:05:14,440
Holy, holy.

66
00:05:14,440 --> 00:05:18,520
Okay, so from now,

67
00:05:18,520 --> 00:05:20,380
let's go, raise your hand if I,

68
00:05:20,380 --> 00:05:22,580
once I named the first video game console

69
00:05:22,580 --> 00:05:23,880
that you had in your house.

70
00:05:23,880 --> 00:05:24,620
Who was the Atari?

71
00:05:24,620 --> 00:05:25,900
Who had Atari first?

72
00:05:25,900 --> 00:05:27,140
Okay, awesome.

73
00:05:27,140 --> 00:05:28,400
You're old and holy.

74
00:05:28,400 --> 00:05:30,720
I'm kidding, I'm kidding.

75
00:05:30,720 --> 00:05:32,540
Nintendo, the original Nintendo.

76
00:05:32,540 --> 00:05:33,940
We got some Nintendo people.

77
00:05:33,940 --> 00:05:34,440
Okay.

78
00:05:34,440 --> 00:05:36,660
How about the Sega Genesis?

79
00:05:37,660 --> 00:05:38,800
All right, all right.

80
00:05:38,800 --> 00:05:40,220
My parents raised their hand over there.

81
00:05:40,220 --> 00:05:41,720
That means that was for me.

82
00:05:41,720 --> 00:05:43,340
The original PlayStation.

83
00:05:43,340 --> 00:05:46,620
All right, now we're getting younger and less holy.

84
00:05:46,620 --> 00:05:47,080
Okay.

85
00:05:47,080 --> 00:05:49,760
The Xbox.

86
00:05:49,760 --> 00:05:51,220
Who was an Xbox person?

87
00:05:51,220 --> 00:05:52,960
I got some Xbox people in the room.

88
00:05:52,960 --> 00:05:55,780
Now, now, are there any,

89
00:05:55,780 --> 00:05:57,480
are there any really young people in here

90
00:05:57,480 --> 00:05:59,020
that would have meant the Nintendo Switch

91
00:05:59,020 --> 00:06:00,480
was like your first game console?

92
00:06:00,480 --> 00:06:01,960
Okay, we got some people here.

93
00:06:02,560 --> 00:06:05,000
Thank you for the young people in the room.

94
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:08,660
I remember one of my most vivid memories

95
00:06:08,660 --> 00:06:10,020
was a Christmas Eve

96
00:06:10,020 --> 00:06:12,880
where my parents had saved up

97
00:06:12,880 --> 00:06:14,080
and surprised my brother and I

98
00:06:14,080 --> 00:06:15,280
with the original PlayStation,

99
00:06:15,280 --> 00:06:18,040
which was really a shock for us.

100
00:06:18,040 --> 00:06:19,700
We didn't, I didn't grow up with a lot of money.

101
00:06:19,700 --> 00:06:22,960
And so this was a huge surprise.

102
00:06:22,960 --> 00:06:24,060
I was really excited about it.

103
00:06:24,060 --> 00:06:25,540
But because we didn't have a lot of money,

104
00:06:25,540 --> 00:06:26,440
there's this thing now,

105
00:06:26,440 --> 00:06:27,740
some of you younger people in the room,

106
00:06:27,740 --> 00:06:28,720
you're not gonna know what this is.

107
00:06:28,720 --> 00:06:31,180
There's this thing called demo discs

108
00:06:31,180 --> 00:06:32,920
that the game came with.

109
00:06:32,920 --> 00:06:35,980
Yeah, my PlayStation came with some demo discs.

110
00:06:35,980 --> 00:06:37,880
And because my parents sacrificially

111
00:06:37,880 --> 00:06:40,140
worked really hard to get us this game,

112
00:06:40,140 --> 00:06:42,440
we spent the first few months playing the demo discs.

113
00:06:42,440 --> 00:06:44,620
We had the console, but not really the games.

114
00:06:44,620 --> 00:06:46,980
I had to wait until the next big holiday

115
00:06:46,980 --> 00:06:49,020
or until I could convince my grandparents

116
00:06:49,020 --> 00:06:49,840
to buy me a game.

117
00:06:49,840 --> 00:06:51,540
So we loved it.

118
00:06:51,540 --> 00:06:54,160
Had this original PlayStation with some demo discs.

119
00:06:54,160 --> 00:06:56,480
And one of the ones I remember most vividly

120
00:06:56,480 --> 00:06:58,700
was a game by the name of Spyro the Dragon.

121
00:06:58,700 --> 00:06:59,220
Anybody?

122
00:06:59,220 --> 00:07:00,040
Okay.

123
00:07:01,040 --> 00:07:03,480
Spyro the Dragon was one of the demo discs.

124
00:07:03,480 --> 00:07:04,780
And I played it on repeat.

125
00:07:04,780 --> 00:07:07,280
You kind of flew this little dragon around.

126
00:07:07,280 --> 00:07:08,520
You could blow fire at enemies.

127
00:07:08,520 --> 00:07:09,520
There he is right there.

128
00:07:09,520 --> 00:07:12,140
You could collect coins

129
00:07:12,140 --> 00:07:13,800
that would help you along the journey.

130
00:07:13,800 --> 00:07:14,880
It was fun at first,

131
00:07:14,880 --> 00:07:16,260
but the demo was contained

132
00:07:16,260 --> 00:07:18,680
to a very small portion of the map.

133
00:07:18,680 --> 00:07:21,000
And there really was no storyline.

134
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:23,660
And there wasn't much that you could do at all

135
00:07:23,660 --> 00:07:25,320
except for fly around and blow fire,

136
00:07:25,320 --> 00:07:27,120
which was fun for about a month,

137
00:07:27,120 --> 00:07:28,180
I will admit.

138
00:07:28,760 --> 00:07:29,940
But then it got boring.

139
00:07:29,940 --> 00:07:32,500
There was not a whole lot there.

140
00:07:32,500 --> 00:07:33,940
I quickly lost interest.

141
00:07:33,940 --> 00:07:35,880
And then eventually we got the real game

142
00:07:35,880 --> 00:07:36,860
and I was a bit skeptical

143
00:07:36,860 --> 00:07:38,900
because I'd been so burnt out by the demo

144
00:07:38,900 --> 00:07:40,100
that I wasn't really sure

145
00:07:40,100 --> 00:07:43,220
that Spyro the Dragon was for me.

146
00:07:43,220 --> 00:07:45,900
And then eventually I gave it a chance

147
00:07:45,900 --> 00:07:46,980
and I was blown away

148
00:07:46,980 --> 00:07:49,720
by how much deeper the real game was to the demo.

149
00:07:49,720 --> 00:07:52,280
There was a storyline that you could follow.

150
00:07:52,420 --> 00:07:55,200
There were hidden trails that you could go along.

151
00:07:55,200 --> 00:07:56,600
There was so much more.

152
00:07:56,600 --> 00:07:59,120
There was different landscapes and hidden paths

153
00:07:59,120 --> 00:08:00,040
and deeper challenges

154
00:08:00,040 --> 00:08:02,800
and a whole story was unfolding.

155
00:08:02,800 --> 00:08:04,600
And this morning,

156
00:08:04,600 --> 00:08:08,460
as we look at John's account of the resurrection,

157
00:08:08,460 --> 00:08:10,620
I wanna make the argument

158
00:08:10,620 --> 00:08:12,440
that I think for many of us,

159
00:08:12,440 --> 00:08:14,240
especially from the gospel of John,

160
00:08:14,240 --> 00:08:15,600
if we've grown up around

161
00:08:15,600 --> 00:08:18,020
the kind of evangelical culture of the day,

162
00:08:18,180 --> 00:08:19,620
we've been given what I would say

163
00:08:19,620 --> 00:08:21,840
is a demo version of the message

164
00:08:21,840 --> 00:08:22,920
of the gospel of Jesus.

165
00:08:22,920 --> 00:08:25,320
It's not untrue.

166
00:08:25,320 --> 00:08:28,280
It's not a part of the message,

167
00:08:28,280 --> 00:08:30,640
but it's shrunken down

168
00:08:30,640 --> 00:08:32,560
and it's missing its entirety.

169
00:08:32,560 --> 00:08:33,980
It's a message that's particularly

170
00:08:33,980 --> 00:08:35,840
about your individual soul

171
00:08:35,840 --> 00:08:37,420
going to heaven when you die.

172
00:08:37,420 --> 00:08:38,740
Again, not untrue,

173
00:08:38,740 --> 00:08:40,780
but it's a demo version

174
00:08:40,780 --> 00:08:43,220
of what John really wants to get across

175
00:08:43,220 --> 00:08:45,680
in his gospel story.

176
00:08:47,740 --> 00:08:49,180
And today from the gospel of John,

177
00:08:49,180 --> 00:08:50,460
I wanna look at a much more full

178
00:08:50,460 --> 00:08:51,600
and beautiful story

179
00:08:51,600 --> 00:08:53,600
of what Jesus actually accomplished

180
00:08:53,600 --> 00:08:54,420
through his life,

181
00:08:54,420 --> 00:08:56,780
death, resurrection, and ascension.

182
00:08:56,780 --> 00:08:58,280
One that isn't limited

183
00:08:58,280 --> 00:09:01,400
to one aspect of our future reality,

184
00:09:01,400 --> 00:09:03,640
but one that infiltrates all creation

185
00:09:03,640 --> 00:09:05,460
and our entire lives.

186
00:09:05,460 --> 00:09:07,180
One that impacts how we live

187
00:09:07,180 --> 00:09:10,860
and breathe and move on a daily basis.

188
00:09:10,860 --> 00:09:16,220
How we interact with God's good world gone wrong

189
00:09:16,220 --> 00:09:17,520
and how we treat one another

190
00:09:17,520 --> 00:09:18,780
in the midst of our suffering

191
00:09:18,780 --> 00:09:20,520
and our tears and our fear

192
00:09:20,520 --> 00:09:21,240
and our regrets.

193
00:09:21,240 --> 00:09:24,880
Easter is the culmination of a story

194
00:09:24,880 --> 00:09:26,000
that has been unfolding

195
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:26,880
since the beginning.

196
00:09:26,880 --> 00:09:27,660
The New Testament

197
00:09:27,660 --> 00:09:31,100
isn't some unexpected add-on

198
00:09:31,100 --> 00:09:33,480
to a story that began with God's creation.

199
00:09:33,480 --> 00:09:34,660
It is the fulfillment

200
00:09:34,660 --> 00:09:35,620
of what we read

201
00:09:35,620 --> 00:09:37,100
on the first pages of Scripture

202
00:09:37,100 --> 00:09:40,440
when God put Adam and Eve

203
00:09:40,440 --> 00:09:42,280
in a good garden.

204
00:09:43,280 --> 00:09:44,620
And what we're gonna find here

205
00:09:44,620 --> 00:09:46,000
as we get to John chapter 20,

206
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:47,200
if you wanna follow along with me,

207
00:09:47,200 --> 00:09:48,400
we're gonna read from there eventually,

208
00:09:48,400 --> 00:09:51,780
is that John goes out of his way.

209
00:09:51,780 --> 00:09:53,820
He's the one gospel author

210
00:09:53,820 --> 00:09:54,840
that goes out of his way

211
00:09:54,840 --> 00:09:56,560
to make sure that you know

212
00:09:56,560 --> 00:09:58,580
that the resurrection happened in a garden.

213
00:09:58,580 --> 00:10:01,360
And he's not doing this on accident.

214
00:10:01,360 --> 00:10:02,440
What he is arguing

215
00:10:02,440 --> 00:10:03,940
is that the message of Jesus,

216
00:10:03,940 --> 00:10:04,780
the resurrection,

217
00:10:04,780 --> 00:10:07,440
is not just about eternal salvation,

218
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:10,440
but it is about new creation bursting forth.

219
00:10:10,440 --> 00:10:13,660
It is about Jesus restoring God's good world

220
00:10:13,660 --> 00:10:16,460
and making the garden of Eden

221
00:10:16,460 --> 00:10:18,180
spread back through creation.

222
00:10:18,180 --> 00:10:20,920
It happens one person at a time

223
00:10:20,920 --> 00:10:22,480
through the power of the Holy Spirit,

224
00:10:22,480 --> 00:10:24,360
but it is spreading.

225
00:10:24,360 --> 00:10:28,280
That's why I've titled my message this morning

226
00:10:28,280 --> 00:10:29,720
From Garden to Garden,

227
00:10:29,720 --> 00:10:33,340
How the Resurrection of Jesus Restores Creation.

228
00:10:33,340 --> 00:10:34,560
And again, with the rest of our time,

229
00:10:34,600 --> 00:10:37,380
I wanna explore some subtle clues from John's gospel

230
00:10:37,380 --> 00:10:39,780
that show us the true story of Jesus

231
00:10:39,780 --> 00:10:41,220
isn't primarily about forgiveness,

232
00:10:41,220 --> 00:10:42,740
but about new creation.

233
00:10:42,740 --> 00:10:43,640
If you have your notes,

234
00:10:43,640 --> 00:10:46,140
you can follow along with me on the back.

235
00:10:46,140 --> 00:10:49,640
I'm gonna start here by looking at how John

236
00:10:49,640 --> 00:10:53,040
revisits the beginning of the story of Scripture

237
00:10:53,040 --> 00:10:54,920
and the beginning of his gospel.

238
00:10:54,920 --> 00:10:57,800
In Genesis chapter one, verses one through three,

239
00:10:57,800 --> 00:10:58,340
we read,

240
00:10:58,340 --> 00:11:02,820
In the beginning, God created the heavens and the earth.

241
00:11:03,560 --> 00:11:05,060
The earth was formless and empty

242
00:11:05,060 --> 00:11:07,140
and darkness covered the deep waters.

243
00:11:07,140 --> 00:11:09,740
Then God said,

244
00:11:09,740 --> 00:11:11,200
Let there be light.

245
00:11:11,200 --> 00:11:12,840
And there was light.

246
00:11:12,840 --> 00:11:15,480
So from the first pages of Scripture,

247
00:11:15,480 --> 00:11:18,000
we have God speaking words

248
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:20,000
that bring light out of darkness.

249
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:23,240
And John begins his gospel

250
00:11:23,240 --> 00:11:25,260
almost in the exact same way.

251
00:11:25,260 --> 00:11:27,900
In John chapter one, verses one through five,

252
00:11:27,900 --> 00:11:28,220
it says,

253
00:11:28,220 --> 00:11:29,440
In the beginning.

254
00:11:29,440 --> 00:11:30,800
Sound familiar?

255
00:11:32,080 --> 00:11:33,860
John's not reinventing the wheel here.

256
00:11:33,860 --> 00:11:36,040
He wants us to have the garden in mind

257
00:11:36,040 --> 00:11:40,600
when he starts his message of the gospel of Jesus.

258
00:11:40,600 --> 00:11:42,840
In the beginning, the word already existed.

259
00:11:42,840 --> 00:11:45,620
The word was with God and the word was God.

260
00:11:45,620 --> 00:11:47,280
God created everything through him

261
00:11:47,280 --> 00:11:50,220
and nothing was created except through him.

262
00:11:50,220 --> 00:11:53,280
The word gave life to everything that was created

263
00:11:53,280 --> 00:11:56,940
and his life brought light to everyone.

264
00:11:57,340 --> 00:12:06,860
So for John, Jesus is the visible expression

265
00:12:06,860 --> 00:12:08,620
of God's spoken word,

266
00:12:08,620 --> 00:12:12,160
bringing light into the darkness of broken creation.

267
00:12:12,160 --> 00:12:14,340
John's claim from the beginning of his book

268
00:12:14,340 --> 00:12:17,640
isn't just Jesus coming to save our souls for eternity,

269
00:12:18,080 --> 00:12:21,440
but God is restarting his good world

270
00:12:21,440 --> 00:12:24,540
through Jesus crushing the head of the serpent.

271
00:12:24,540 --> 00:12:28,000
He's restoring the goodness of the garden of Eden.

272
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:30,180
He came to undo the lies of the enemy

273
00:12:30,180 --> 00:12:32,160
that lead us away from God,

274
00:12:32,160 --> 00:12:33,780
lies that lead us to selfishness,

275
00:12:33,780 --> 00:12:35,120
dehumanization, destruction.

276
00:12:35,120 --> 00:12:36,660
This is where sin comes into the world

277
00:12:36,660 --> 00:12:38,760
because we believe the lies of the enemy.

278
00:12:38,760 --> 00:12:41,760
We believe that the way of the enemy will lead to life

279
00:12:41,760 --> 00:12:44,040
when in reality, it leads to death and destruction.

280
00:12:44,640 --> 00:12:47,740
And Jesus is shining a light on a new way of being human.

281
00:12:47,740 --> 00:12:52,000
John's gospel is filled with clues

282
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:54,700
that he's primarily talking about new creation

283
00:12:54,700 --> 00:12:57,160
and not about just where we go when we die.

284
00:12:57,160 --> 00:12:59,640
But because I don't have all mourning,

285
00:12:59,640 --> 00:13:02,280
we're not gonna trace all of John's clues.

286
00:13:02,280 --> 00:13:03,320
We're just gonna skip ahead

287
00:13:03,320 --> 00:13:06,220
to the crucifixion and resurrection.

288
00:13:06,220 --> 00:13:09,900
In the first section, we see these similarities

289
00:13:09,900 --> 00:13:13,260
where John kind of compares the beginning of his letter

290
00:13:13,260 --> 00:13:14,860
to the beginning of the book of Genesis.

291
00:13:14,860 --> 00:13:17,420
And as we move along, we'll see some more comparisons

292
00:13:17,420 --> 00:13:20,700
and also some ways that they contrast one another.

293
00:13:20,700 --> 00:13:25,340
He moves on to focus on the brokenness of creation.

294
00:13:25,340 --> 00:13:27,600
In Genesis chapter one, verse 27, it says,

295
00:13:27,600 --> 00:13:30,240
in the image of God, he created them,

296
00:13:30,240 --> 00:13:32,800
male and female, he created them.

297
00:13:32,800 --> 00:13:35,380
So in Genesis, we have God creating Adam and Eve

298
00:13:35,380 --> 00:13:38,640
and declaring that these humans were made in his image.

299
00:13:38,640 --> 00:13:42,460
They are representations of all of humanity moving forward.

300
00:13:42,460 --> 00:13:44,320
And when they fail, we all fail.

301
00:13:44,320 --> 00:13:47,500
And then you have this really weird line

302
00:13:47,500 --> 00:13:50,400
that John shares in John chapter 19, verse five,

303
00:13:50,400 --> 00:13:53,560
where Pilate brings out Jesus to the crowd.

304
00:13:53,560 --> 00:13:57,840
And he says, look, here is the man.

305
00:13:57,840 --> 00:13:59,420
Isn't that weird phrasing?

306
00:13:59,420 --> 00:14:01,940
You ever been reading through the Scriptures

307
00:14:01,940 --> 00:14:04,460
and something, there's like a weird way of saying something.

308
00:14:04,460 --> 00:14:06,400
You're like, the translators must've really messed up there.

309
00:14:06,900 --> 00:14:09,940
If you see something that looks weird like that,

310
00:14:09,940 --> 00:14:13,740
zoom in on it a little bit and figure out why it is weird.

311
00:14:13,740 --> 00:14:16,700
I think what we have here is we have,

312
00:14:16,700 --> 00:14:21,080
in Genesis, we have God bringing out Adam and Eve and saying,

313
00:14:21,080 --> 00:14:23,560
this is humanity created in my image.

314
00:14:23,560 --> 00:14:26,000
This is what goodness looks like.

315
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:28,420
And then in John, we have Pilate.

316
00:14:28,420 --> 00:14:31,860
We have the empire proclaiming Jesus as the true image bearer

317
00:14:31,860 --> 00:14:33,220
without knowing what they're doing.

318
00:14:33,220 --> 00:14:36,540
Pilate is proclaiming Jesus as the new Adam,

319
00:14:36,540 --> 00:14:38,720
representing all of humanity

320
00:14:38,720 --> 00:14:41,140
and going to the cross on our behalf,

321
00:14:41,140 --> 00:14:45,420
taking death and restoring dominion in the garden.

322
00:14:45,420 --> 00:14:48,160
It moves on in Genesis chapter three

323
00:14:48,160 --> 00:14:51,760
as the curse comes onto creation after humanity sins.

324
00:14:51,760 --> 00:14:52,920
It says, God says,

325
00:14:53,000 --> 00:15:13,840
This is death entering God's good world,

326
00:15:13,840 --> 00:15:16,260
focused on thorns and the sweat of our brow

327
00:15:16,260 --> 00:15:19,000
and fear and the brokenness of other people

328
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:20,460
warring against one another.

329
00:15:20,460 --> 00:15:24,680
And in John 19, we see the soldiers wove a crown of thorns

330
00:15:24,680 --> 00:15:27,680
and put it on his head and the crowd chanted,

331
00:15:27,680 --> 00:15:30,000
crucify him, crucify him.

332
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:32,880
John wants us to have in mind creation

333
00:15:32,880 --> 00:15:36,120
as we see what Jesus is doing on our behalf.

334
00:15:36,120 --> 00:15:41,740
He is the new image of God doing in a desert

335
00:15:41,740 --> 00:15:44,240
what Adam and Eve could not do in the garden.

336
00:15:44,240 --> 00:15:49,240
Jesus is taking on the curse of death.

337
00:15:49,860 --> 00:15:51,180
And overcoming it.

338
00:15:51,180 --> 00:15:54,120
In Genesis chapter two,

339
00:15:54,120 --> 00:15:56,840
we read that in the middle of the garden,

340
00:15:56,840 --> 00:15:58,520
God placed the tree of life

341
00:15:58,520 --> 00:16:01,540
and the tree of the knowledge of good and evil.

342
00:16:01,540 --> 00:16:03,740
These trees were intended for life

343
00:16:03,740 --> 00:16:05,780
and flourishing a mutually good

344
00:16:05,780 --> 00:16:08,400
and beneficial relationship between humans and God.

345
00:16:08,400 --> 00:16:10,540
But it was the tree in the middle of the garden

346
00:16:10,540 --> 00:16:13,140
that ultimately led to our death and chaos.

347
00:16:13,140 --> 00:16:15,520
And then John is the only gospel author

348
00:16:15,520 --> 00:16:18,780
that goes out of his way to describe Jesus's cross

349
00:16:18,780 --> 00:16:22,500
as being in the middle of the crucifixion.

350
00:16:22,500 --> 00:16:23,820
In John 19,

351
00:16:23,820 --> 00:16:27,020
then Pilate turned Jesus over to him to be crucified.

352
00:16:27,020 --> 00:16:29,860
They took Jesus away, carrying the cross by himself.

353
00:16:29,860 --> 00:16:32,220
He went to the place called the place of skull.

354
00:16:32,220 --> 00:16:34,280
So we've got a tree in the middle of the garden

355
00:16:34,280 --> 00:16:36,720
and now we have a tree in the middle of the desert.

356
00:16:37,260 --> 00:16:38,760
There they nailed him to the cross.

357
00:16:38,760 --> 00:16:40,260
Two others were crucified with him,

358
00:16:40,260 --> 00:16:43,480
one on either side with Jesus in the middle.

359
00:16:43,480 --> 00:16:47,300
John uses the same Greek word

360
00:16:47,300 --> 00:16:49,160
that the Septuagint translates,

361
00:16:49,160 --> 00:16:51,020
the tree in the middle of the garden.

362
00:16:51,020 --> 00:16:53,480
He wants us to have the garden in mind.

363
00:16:53,540 --> 00:16:56,360
He wants us to see that when Adam and Eve failed

364
00:16:56,360 --> 00:16:58,300
in the midst of the garden with a tree,

365
00:16:58,300 --> 00:17:01,840
Jesus succeeded in the midst of the desert on a cross.

366
00:17:01,840 --> 00:17:05,180
Jesus steps into the world of Genesis 3

367
00:17:05,180 --> 00:17:06,260
outside of the garden.

368
00:17:06,260 --> 00:17:08,720
His ministry culminates in him being stripped naked,

369
00:17:08,720 --> 00:17:10,600
beaten and killed for a crime

370
00:17:10,600 --> 00:17:12,340
that he did not commit on a tree

371
00:17:12,340 --> 00:17:14,500
in the middle of a place called the skull.

372
00:17:14,500 --> 00:17:18,020
Jesus steps outside of the garden

373
00:17:18,020 --> 00:17:20,760
to overcome the lies of the enemy that we believe,

374
00:17:20,760 --> 00:17:23,100
that got us removed from the garden.

375
00:17:23,100 --> 00:17:25,320
And he did this to open up a door for us

376
00:17:25,320 --> 00:17:28,500
to experience the garden life again.

377
00:17:28,500 --> 00:17:31,520
This is not a demo version of the gospel.

378
00:17:31,520 --> 00:17:33,340
John does not just want you to think about

379
00:17:33,340 --> 00:17:35,340
your individual sins being forgiven.

380
00:17:35,340 --> 00:17:36,260
He wants you to think about

381
00:17:36,260 --> 00:17:38,360
all of creation being restored.

382
00:17:38,360 --> 00:17:42,000
Sometimes we shrink what Jesus did down so much

383
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:43,960
that we miss the grand scheme

384
00:17:43,960 --> 00:17:46,620
of all that God is doing through Jesus.

385
00:17:46,620 --> 00:17:50,080
And I am preaching better than you guys are responding.

386
00:17:52,660 --> 00:17:55,940
For John, the crucifixion is the culmination

387
00:17:55,940 --> 00:17:57,160
of a world and rebellion.

388
00:17:57,160 --> 00:17:59,080
This is as bad as it can get.

389
00:17:59,080 --> 00:18:03,080
Humanity is crucifying God on a cross

390
00:18:03,080 --> 00:18:04,700
in the middle of the desert.

391
00:18:04,700 --> 00:18:08,560
For John, this is as bad as it can get

392
00:18:08,560 --> 00:18:10,100
and everything is about to turn around.

393
00:18:10,100 --> 00:18:12,520
Jesus is putting an end to the lies of the enemy

394
00:18:12,520 --> 00:18:14,180
that have led humanity down this path.

395
00:18:14,180 --> 00:18:15,900
He is crushing the head of the serpent

396
00:18:15,900 --> 00:18:19,720
and providing a new way for humans to relate to God.

397
00:18:19,800 --> 00:18:21,940
He's kick-starting new creation.

398
00:18:21,940 --> 00:18:26,840
Self-giving love is greater than selfish violence and greed.

399
00:18:26,840 --> 00:18:34,280
And then we zoom in on the resurrection account.

400
00:18:34,280 --> 00:18:36,740
I'm just gonna read the whole thing

401
00:18:36,740 --> 00:18:39,360
because I think we should do that on Easter

402
00:18:39,360 --> 00:18:42,120
and then we'll come back and grab a couple of highlights.

403
00:18:42,120 --> 00:18:43,780
There's more than I have time to cover.

404
00:18:43,920 --> 00:18:46,180
And so I would encourage you this week

405
00:18:46,180 --> 00:18:47,800
if you wanna read John 20 and 21

406
00:18:47,800 --> 00:18:49,680
with the Garden of Eden in your mind

407
00:18:49,680 --> 00:18:50,960
and try and see some of the ways

408
00:18:50,960 --> 00:18:52,600
in which John wants us to think about

409
00:18:52,600 --> 00:18:54,540
Jesus kick-starting new creation.

410
00:18:54,540 --> 00:18:59,480
Wait, I might have gotten ahead on my notes.

411
00:18:59,480 --> 00:19:00,040
I did.

412
00:19:00,040 --> 00:19:01,020
I got ahead.

413
00:19:01,020 --> 00:19:02,380
We're not gonna read that yet.

414
00:19:03,200 --> 00:19:06,180
So what happens when you guys don't respond well enough?

415
00:19:06,180 --> 00:19:08,080
I try and skip pages of my notes.

416
00:19:08,080 --> 00:19:10,980
All right, the turning point.

417
00:19:10,980 --> 00:19:13,420
As Jesus is being crucified,

418
00:19:13,420 --> 00:19:16,460
in this section, John clearly wants us to see

419
00:19:16,460 --> 00:19:17,940
how Christ's work of new creation

420
00:19:17,940 --> 00:19:21,220
mirrors God's work in the original creation account.

421
00:19:21,220 --> 00:19:23,240
On the sixth day in Genesis chapter one,

422
00:19:23,240 --> 00:19:24,940
God looked over all that he had made

423
00:19:24,940 --> 00:19:26,300
and he saw that it was very good,

424
00:19:26,300 --> 00:19:29,320
marking the sixth day, Friday in the week.

425
00:19:30,220 --> 00:19:32,220
In John chapter 19,

426
00:19:32,220 --> 00:19:36,340
Jesus finishes the work necessary for new creation

427
00:19:36,340 --> 00:19:38,780
on the sixth day.

428
00:19:38,780 --> 00:19:40,820
It is finished, he says.

429
00:19:40,820 --> 00:19:43,160
John says it was the day of preparation.

430
00:19:43,160 --> 00:19:45,520
John goes out of his way to let us know

431
00:19:45,520 --> 00:19:47,360
the days and the times of things happening.

432
00:19:47,360 --> 00:19:49,900
And then on the seventh day,

433
00:19:49,900 --> 00:19:52,760
when God had finished all of his good creation

434
00:19:52,760 --> 00:19:55,880
in the garden, he rested from all his work.

435
00:19:57,560 --> 00:19:59,200
In John chapter 19,

436
00:19:59,200 --> 00:20:03,980
the place of crucifixion was near a garden

437
00:20:03,980 --> 00:20:07,820
where there was a new tomb, never used before.

438
00:20:07,820 --> 00:20:11,340
And so before, because it was the day of preparation

439
00:20:11,340 --> 00:20:12,340
for the Jewish Passover

440
00:20:12,340 --> 00:20:14,220
and since the tomb was close at hand,

441
00:20:14,220 --> 00:20:16,960
they laid Jesus there.

442
00:20:16,960 --> 00:20:21,580
Jesus, who is God,

443
00:20:21,580 --> 00:20:25,360
completed the work of new creation on the sixth day

444
00:20:25,360 --> 00:20:27,320
and rested in the tomb on the seventh.

445
00:20:27,320 --> 00:20:32,460
This is new creation coming about

446
00:20:32,460 --> 00:20:34,100
through the sacrificial love,

447
00:20:34,100 --> 00:20:35,680
through the life, death, burial,

448
00:20:35,680 --> 00:20:37,000
and resurrection of Jesus.

449
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:39,420
The gospel of John is a literary masterpiece.

450
00:20:39,420 --> 00:20:41,760
He puts the image of the Garden of Eden

451
00:20:41,760 --> 00:20:43,480
in our minds in chapter one.

452
00:20:43,480 --> 00:20:46,260
And the entire story leads us back to a garden

453
00:20:46,260 --> 00:20:48,620
to show us that Jesus is launching new creation.

454
00:20:48,620 --> 00:20:50,660
This is so much better than the demo mode

455
00:20:50,660 --> 00:20:52,920
of the gospel that many of us have in our minds

456
00:20:52,920 --> 00:20:54,360
when we think about what Jesus did.

457
00:20:54,360 --> 00:20:56,460
Light is bursting through the darkness

458
00:20:56,460 --> 00:20:59,240
and we are being invited into a totally new way

459
00:20:59,240 --> 00:21:00,940
of being human.

460
00:21:00,940 --> 00:21:05,040
Now, let's get to the resurrection account.

461
00:21:05,040 --> 00:21:10,440
We've got new creation being finished on the sixth day,

462
00:21:10,440 --> 00:21:12,100
Jesus resting on the seventh day,

463
00:21:12,100 --> 00:21:13,740
and John goes out of his way

464
00:21:13,740 --> 00:21:18,540
to mention that this is the first day of new creation.

465
00:21:18,940 --> 00:21:21,000
This is why we gather together on Sunday morning.

466
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:24,220
Sunday marks the first day of new creation.

467
00:21:24,220 --> 00:21:26,160
Now, on the first day of the week,

468
00:21:26,160 --> 00:21:28,160
Mary Magdalene came to the tomb early

469
00:21:28,160 --> 00:21:30,580
while it was still dark.

470
00:21:30,580 --> 00:21:32,640
On the first day of creation,

471
00:21:32,640 --> 00:21:34,620
light is coming through the darkness.

472
00:21:34,620 --> 00:21:39,560
And she saw the stone had been taken away from the tomb,

473
00:21:39,560 --> 00:21:41,340
so she ran and went to Simon Peter

474
00:21:41,340 --> 00:21:42,160
and the other disciple,

475
00:21:42,160 --> 00:21:43,420
the one whom Jesus loved.

476
00:21:43,420 --> 00:21:45,720
John has a really interesting way

477
00:21:45,720 --> 00:21:47,120
of talking about himself and Peter

478
00:21:47,120 --> 00:21:48,580
that I don't have time to get into.

479
00:21:48,580 --> 00:21:50,560
And he said to them,

480
00:21:50,560 --> 00:21:52,300
they have taken the Lord out of the tomb

481
00:21:52,300 --> 00:21:54,100
and we do not know where they have laid him.

482
00:21:54,100 --> 00:21:56,220
So Peter went out with the other disciple.

483
00:21:56,220 --> 00:21:57,540
They were going towards the tomb.

484
00:21:57,540 --> 00:21:58,800
Both of them were running together,

485
00:21:58,800 --> 00:22:00,720
but the other disciple outran Peter

486
00:22:00,720 --> 00:22:03,940
and reached the tomb first.

487
00:22:03,940 --> 00:22:05,760
Stooping to look in,

488
00:22:05,760 --> 00:22:07,620
he saw the linen clothes lying there,

489
00:22:07,620 --> 00:22:08,860
but he did not go in.

490
00:22:08,860 --> 00:22:10,580
Then Simon Peter came following him

491
00:22:10,580 --> 00:22:11,560
and went into the tomb.

492
00:22:12,080 --> 00:22:13,860
He saw the linen clothes lying there

493
00:22:13,860 --> 00:22:15,460
and the face cloth,

494
00:22:15,460 --> 00:22:17,300
which had been on Jesus' head,

495
00:22:17,300 --> 00:22:18,680
not lying with the linen clothes,

496
00:22:18,680 --> 00:22:20,340
but folded up in its place.

497
00:22:20,340 --> 00:22:21,780
Then the other disciple

498
00:22:21,780 --> 00:22:23,080
who had reached the tomb first,

499
00:22:23,080 --> 00:22:24,600
again, John, chill,

500
00:22:24,600 --> 00:22:28,760
also went in and he saw and believed,

501
00:22:28,760 --> 00:22:30,900
for as yet they did not understand the Scripture

502
00:22:30,900 --> 00:22:32,380
that he must rise from the dead.

503
00:22:32,380 --> 00:22:34,180
Then the disciples went back to their homes.

504
00:22:34,180 --> 00:22:38,340
But Mary stood weeping outside the tomb

505
00:22:38,340 --> 00:22:39,520
and she wept.

506
00:22:39,640 --> 00:22:41,400
She stood and looked into the tomb.

507
00:22:41,400 --> 00:22:43,260
She saw two angels in white sitting

508
00:22:43,260 --> 00:22:44,940
where the body of Jesus had laid,

509
00:22:44,940 --> 00:22:47,140
one at the head and one at the feet.

510
00:22:47,140 --> 00:22:48,340
They said to her,

511
00:22:48,340 --> 00:22:49,840
woman, why are you weeping?

512
00:22:49,840 --> 00:22:51,260
She said to them,

513
00:22:51,260 --> 00:22:52,700
they have taken away my Lord

514
00:22:52,700 --> 00:22:54,520
and I do not know where they have laid him.

515
00:22:54,520 --> 00:22:56,120
Having said this,

516
00:22:56,120 --> 00:22:58,440
she turned around and she saw Jesus,

517
00:22:58,440 --> 00:23:00,920
but she did not know it was him.

518
00:23:00,920 --> 00:23:02,740
Jesus said to her,

519
00:23:02,740 --> 00:23:03,840
woman, why are you weeping?

520
00:23:03,840 --> 00:23:04,680
Whom are you seeking?

521
00:23:04,680 --> 00:23:07,480
Supposing him to be the gardener,

522
00:23:07,480 --> 00:23:08,240
she said to him,

523
00:23:08,240 --> 00:23:09,800
sir, if you have carried him away,

524
00:23:09,800 --> 00:23:11,340
tell me where you have laid him

525
00:23:11,340 --> 00:23:12,940
and I will take him away.

526
00:23:12,940 --> 00:23:14,820
Jesus said to her,

527
00:23:14,820 --> 00:23:15,740
Mary.

528
00:23:15,740 --> 00:23:19,180
She turned and said to him in Aramaic,

529
00:23:19,180 --> 00:23:20,700
Rabboni, which means teacher.

530
00:23:20,700 --> 00:23:22,820
Jesus said to her,

531
00:23:22,820 --> 00:23:23,780
do not cling to me

532
00:23:23,780 --> 00:23:25,780
for I have not yet ascended to the father,

533
00:23:25,780 --> 00:23:27,620
but go to my brothers and say to them,

534
00:23:27,620 --> 00:23:29,060
I am ascending to my father

535
00:23:29,060 --> 00:23:30,440
and to your father,

536
00:23:30,440 --> 00:23:32,320
my God and your God.

537
00:23:32,320 --> 00:23:35,420
Mary Magdalene went and announced to the disciples,

538
00:23:35,420 --> 00:23:37,380
I have seen the Lord

539
00:23:37,380 --> 00:23:42,020
and that he said these things to her.

540
00:23:42,020 --> 00:23:44,200
On the evening of that day,

541
00:23:44,200 --> 00:23:45,960
the first day of new creation,

542
00:23:45,960 --> 00:23:47,140
the doors being locked

543
00:23:47,140 --> 00:23:49,380
where the disciples were for fear of the Jews,

544
00:23:49,380 --> 00:23:51,120
Jesus came and stood among them

545
00:23:51,120 --> 00:23:51,960
and he said to them,

546
00:23:51,960 --> 00:23:52,880
peace be with you.

547
00:23:52,880 --> 00:23:54,320
When he said this,

548
00:23:54,320 --> 00:23:56,060
he showed them his hands and his side.

549
00:23:56,060 --> 00:23:57,600
Then the disciples were glad

550
00:23:57,600 --> 00:23:59,080
when they saw the Lord.

551
00:23:59,080 --> 00:24:00,360
Jesus said to them again,

552
00:24:00,360 --> 00:24:01,660
peace be with you

553
00:24:01,660 --> 00:24:03,020
as the father has sent me,

554
00:24:03,020 --> 00:24:04,640
even so I am sending you.

555
00:24:04,640 --> 00:24:06,580
And when he had said this,

556
00:24:06,580 --> 00:24:09,000
he breathed on them

557
00:24:09,000 --> 00:24:10,580
and said to them,

558
00:24:10,580 --> 00:24:12,680
receive the Holy Spirit.

559
00:24:12,680 --> 00:24:15,720
So again,

560
00:24:15,720 --> 00:24:18,140
with the garden imagery in our minds,

561
00:24:18,140 --> 00:24:20,660
John goes out of his way to say,

562
00:24:20,660 --> 00:24:22,380
this is the first day of new creation

563
00:24:22,380 --> 00:24:23,540
and it is in darkness

564
00:24:23,540 --> 00:24:25,040
and the word of God,

565
00:24:25,040 --> 00:24:27,300
light is spreading out from Jesus

566
00:24:27,300 --> 00:24:29,480
on the first day of new creation.

567
00:24:29,480 --> 00:24:30,760
light is dawning,

568
00:24:30,760 --> 00:24:32,340
hope has come.

569
00:24:32,340 --> 00:24:35,620
When the curse happens in the garden,

570
00:24:35,620 --> 00:24:37,940
you see human beings hiding from God.

571
00:24:37,940 --> 00:24:41,000
And in this account,

572
00:24:41,000 --> 00:24:43,100
we see Mary searching for God.

573
00:24:43,100 --> 00:24:46,800
New creation is dawning.

574
00:24:46,800 --> 00:24:49,420
Human beings are beginning to catch a vision

575
00:24:49,420 --> 00:24:50,680
for what life could look like

576
00:24:50,680 --> 00:24:52,560
in relationship with God and one another.

577
00:24:52,560 --> 00:24:55,420
I got a deep cut for those of you

578
00:24:55,420 --> 00:24:56,460
that grew up in Sunday school.

579
00:24:56,460 --> 00:24:59,180
We got time for it real quick?

580
00:25:00,320 --> 00:25:00,600
All right,

581
00:25:00,600 --> 00:25:02,220
you notice we had two angels

582
00:25:02,220 --> 00:25:04,420
on either side of where Jesus laid?

583
00:25:04,420 --> 00:25:08,300
So the deep cut is,

584
00:25:08,300 --> 00:25:09,240
in the Old Testament,

585
00:25:09,240 --> 00:25:11,080
we have the description of the tabernacle,

586
00:25:11,080 --> 00:25:12,520
which all theologians agree

587
00:25:12,520 --> 00:25:14,460
is a working model of Eden,

588
00:25:14,460 --> 00:25:15,400
the Garden of Eden,

589
00:25:15,400 --> 00:25:17,260
wherever Israel would go.

590
00:25:17,260 --> 00:25:18,140
In the midst of Israel,

591
00:25:18,140 --> 00:25:20,340
it's God's presence dwelling with his people

592
00:25:20,340 --> 00:25:21,880
just like he did in the garden.

593
00:25:21,880 --> 00:25:23,700
And at the center of the tabernacle,

594
00:25:23,700 --> 00:25:25,260
you have a place called the mercy seat

595
00:25:25,260 --> 00:25:26,960
inside the Holy of Holies.

596
00:25:27,520 --> 00:25:29,520
And what is on the mercy seat?

597
00:25:29,520 --> 00:25:32,820
You have an angel on either side of the mercy seat

598
00:25:32,820 --> 00:25:34,380
where the presence of God

599
00:25:34,380 --> 00:25:36,240
dwells in the midst of his people.

600
00:25:36,240 --> 00:25:37,620
And when John says here,

601
00:25:37,620 --> 00:25:39,080
there's an angel on either side

602
00:25:39,080 --> 00:25:39,960
of where Jesus laid,

603
00:25:39,960 --> 00:25:42,640
he's not just giving details that don't matter.

604
00:25:42,640 --> 00:25:44,400
He's asking the people of God

605
00:25:44,400 --> 00:25:45,640
who know the story of God

606
00:25:45,640 --> 00:25:47,800
to know that the presence of God

607
00:25:47,800 --> 00:25:48,860
was dwelling there

608
00:25:48,860 --> 00:25:50,840
and he has risen from the dead

609
00:25:50,840 --> 00:25:52,500
and he is here now

610
00:25:52,500 --> 00:25:54,420
and new creation is dawning.

611
00:25:54,420 --> 00:25:56,480
This small working model of creation

612
00:25:56,480 --> 00:25:57,960
that can only be with Israel

613
00:25:57,960 --> 00:26:00,360
and this tent is no longer matters

614
00:26:00,360 --> 00:26:02,700
because God is spreading the garden

615
00:26:02,700 --> 00:26:04,560
all throughout the rest of the world.

616
00:26:04,560 --> 00:26:09,880
First day, humans go looking for God.

617
00:26:09,880 --> 00:26:11,280
God's presence is there.

618
00:26:11,280 --> 00:26:13,000
And I love in Genesis,

619
00:26:13,000 --> 00:26:15,160
we have God planting the garden.

620
00:26:16,220 --> 00:26:17,160
And in John 20,

621
00:26:17,160 --> 00:26:19,880
we have Jesus mistaken for the gardener.

622
00:26:19,880 --> 00:26:22,520
What a small detail that John has here

623
00:26:22,520 --> 00:26:24,200
as almost to say like you,

624
00:26:24,200 --> 00:26:26,220
mistaken as the gardener,

625
00:26:26,220 --> 00:26:27,960
but no, he actually is the gardener.

626
00:26:29,660 --> 00:26:32,820
He is bringing the garden of Eden

627
00:26:32,820 --> 00:26:35,480
back to this broken world.

628
00:26:35,480 --> 00:26:38,440
When we pray on earth as it is in heaven,

629
00:26:38,440 --> 00:26:40,880
it's not just this spiritual reality

630
00:26:40,880 --> 00:26:42,260
that we hope to be true in the future.

631
00:26:42,260 --> 00:26:45,180
It is an invitation for us to participate in God,

632
00:26:45,180 --> 00:26:48,120
bringing new creation through his people,

633
00:26:48,120 --> 00:26:49,340
his new creation.

634
00:26:49,340 --> 00:26:52,900
And the last thing that happened

635
00:26:52,900 --> 00:26:54,520
on the first day of new creation

636
00:26:54,520 --> 00:26:56,860
is Jesus breathes on the disciples

637
00:26:56,860 --> 00:26:58,860
the breath of new life.

638
00:27:00,660 --> 00:27:01,900
Just as in Genesis,

639
00:27:01,900 --> 00:27:05,160
God breathed life into Adam.

640
00:27:05,160 --> 00:27:06,780
It says he breathed on Adam,

641
00:27:06,780 --> 00:27:07,620
the breath of life.

642
00:27:07,620 --> 00:27:09,740
The last thing that John goes out of his way

643
00:27:09,740 --> 00:27:10,500
to say that happened

644
00:27:10,500 --> 00:27:11,920
on the first day of new creation

645
00:27:11,920 --> 00:27:13,860
is Jesus breathed on his disciples.

646
00:27:13,860 --> 00:27:15,100
Have you ever read that

647
00:27:15,100 --> 00:27:16,060
and been like, that's weird?

648
00:27:16,060 --> 00:27:18,740
Somebody just, my friend,

649
00:27:18,740 --> 00:27:20,180
if Corey just walked up to me

650
00:27:20,180 --> 00:27:20,940
and breathed on me,

651
00:27:20,940 --> 00:27:22,960
I'd be like, dude, get away from me.

652
00:27:22,960 --> 00:27:26,580
It's not like there's some first century thing

653
00:27:26,580 --> 00:27:27,240
we don't know about

654
00:27:27,240 --> 00:27:28,140
where people were just gone

655
00:27:28,140 --> 00:27:29,260
breathing on each other.

656
00:27:29,340 --> 00:27:32,540
No, John is going out of his way

657
00:27:32,540 --> 00:27:35,540
to say that Jesus is God

658
00:27:35,540 --> 00:27:38,320
and he is bringing about new creation

659
00:27:38,320 --> 00:27:40,540
and he is breathing new life

660
00:27:40,540 --> 00:27:42,080
into the new human beings

661
00:27:42,080 --> 00:27:43,040
who will trust him,

662
00:27:43,040 --> 00:27:44,540
who will follow him,

663
00:27:44,540 --> 00:27:45,200
who will say,

664
00:27:45,200 --> 00:27:46,780
the enemy has been crushed.

665
00:27:46,780 --> 00:27:48,900
I no longer have to believe the lies

666
00:27:48,900 --> 00:27:50,840
that lead to fear, dehumanization

667
00:27:50,840 --> 00:27:52,460
and warring against one another.

668
00:27:52,460 --> 00:27:54,240
I can now live open-handedly

669
00:27:54,240 --> 00:27:55,120
with my abundance.

670
00:27:55,120 --> 00:27:56,100
I can love God

671
00:27:56,100 --> 00:27:58,100
with all of my heart, soul, mind and strength.

672
00:27:58,100 --> 00:27:59,900
And I can love my neighbor as myself.

673
00:27:59,900 --> 00:28:01,600
This is how the garden spreads

674
00:28:01,600 --> 00:28:03,920
from here until Jesus returns.

675
00:28:03,920 --> 00:28:05,200
Us, new humans

676
00:28:05,200 --> 00:28:06,440
with the power of the Holy Spirit

677
00:28:06,440 --> 00:28:07,340
living inside of us,

678
00:28:07,340 --> 00:28:08,700
loving the Lord our God

679
00:28:08,700 --> 00:28:09,980
with our heart, soul, mind and strength

680
00:28:09,980 --> 00:28:12,160
and loving our neighbor as ourself.

681
00:28:12,160 --> 00:28:13,400
For John,

682
00:28:13,400 --> 00:28:14,380
the good news of Jesus

683
00:28:14,380 --> 00:28:15,420
is that the garden

684
00:28:15,420 --> 00:28:16,380
is beginning again

685
00:28:16,380 --> 00:28:17,300
and human beings

686
00:28:17,300 --> 00:28:18,480
are invited to participate.

687
00:28:19,300 --> 00:28:20,260
Fellowship with God

688
00:28:20,260 --> 00:28:20,840
is restored

689
00:28:20,840 --> 00:28:21,500
and partnership

690
00:28:21,500 --> 00:28:22,240
with one another

691
00:28:22,240 --> 00:28:24,100
is now a realistic possibility.

692
00:28:24,100 --> 00:28:26,440
This version of the gospel

693
00:28:26,440 --> 00:28:27,640
blows the demo mode

694
00:28:27,640 --> 00:28:28,360
out of the water.

695
00:28:28,360 --> 00:28:29,700
It's not just about forgiveness

696
00:28:29,700 --> 00:28:30,280
of sins

697
00:28:30,280 --> 00:28:31,320
or future destination.

698
00:28:31,320 --> 00:28:32,620
It's about here

699
00:28:32,620 --> 00:28:33,440
and now.

700
00:28:33,440 --> 00:28:34,840
Every breath we take

701
00:28:34,840 --> 00:28:35,500
is an invitation

702
00:28:35,500 --> 00:28:36,820
to partner with God

703
00:28:36,820 --> 00:28:38,300
to bring about his good world

704
00:28:38,300 --> 00:28:39,480
gone wrong.

705
00:28:39,480 --> 00:28:40,840
The gospel

706
00:28:40,840 --> 00:28:42,160
isn't just about eternal life

707
00:28:42,160 --> 00:28:44,400
but abundant life now.

708
00:28:46,900 --> 00:28:48,140
You guys are getting there.

709
00:28:48,140 --> 00:28:49,600
I appreciate it.

710
00:28:49,600 --> 00:28:52,700
So like I said earlier,

711
00:28:52,700 --> 00:28:54,740
I quickly burn out

712
00:28:54,740 --> 00:28:56,300
on the demo mode of Spyro

713
00:28:56,300 --> 00:28:58,520
and I was a bit skeptical

714
00:28:58,520 --> 00:29:00,080
that the real game was for me.

715
00:29:00,080 --> 00:29:04,660
And I can't help but think

716
00:29:04,660 --> 00:29:05,580
that there are some of us

717
00:29:05,580 --> 00:29:06,340
in the room today

718
00:29:06,340 --> 00:29:07,180
that have grown up

719
00:29:07,180 --> 00:29:08,460
with kind of a demo version

720
00:29:08,460 --> 00:29:09,220
of the gospel.

721
00:29:09,220 --> 00:29:13,320
Jesus died for your sins.

722
00:29:13,320 --> 00:29:14,400
Ask him into your heart.

723
00:29:14,400 --> 00:29:16,040
You go to heaven when you die.

724
00:29:16,400 --> 00:29:17,720
Again, not untrue

725
00:29:17,720 --> 00:29:20,020
but just one facet

726
00:29:20,020 --> 00:29:21,340
of all that Jesus is doing

727
00:29:21,340 --> 00:29:22,040
and wants to do

728
00:29:22,040 --> 00:29:23,500
in your life here and now.

729
00:29:23,500 --> 00:29:25,420
And I can't help but think

730
00:29:25,420 --> 00:29:26,160
that there are people

731
00:29:26,160 --> 00:29:27,320
in the room this morning

732
00:29:27,320 --> 00:29:29,020
who might be thinking

733
00:29:29,020 --> 00:29:29,700
like me

734
00:29:29,700 --> 00:29:31,720
that Spyro isn't for me.

735
00:29:31,720 --> 00:29:32,380
You might be thinking,

736
00:29:32,380 --> 00:29:33,440
yeah, this gospel thing,

737
00:29:33,440 --> 00:29:34,380
this Jesus raising

738
00:29:34,380 --> 00:29:35,060
from the dead thing,

739
00:29:35,060 --> 00:29:35,860
it sounds great.

740
00:29:35,860 --> 00:29:36,860
It's nice for the people

741
00:29:36,860 --> 00:29:37,740
that it's nice for

742
00:29:37,740 --> 00:29:38,660
but it's not for me.

743
00:29:38,660 --> 00:29:42,520
And if that's you,

744
00:29:42,520 --> 00:29:43,100
if you're in here,

745
00:29:43,100 --> 00:29:43,740
if you're skeptical,

746
00:29:43,960 --> 00:29:45,100
if you have reasons

747
00:29:45,100 --> 00:29:46,720
for not believing

748
00:29:46,720 --> 00:29:47,740
or not wanting to believe

749
00:29:47,740 --> 00:29:48,780
or maybe you want to believe

750
00:29:48,780 --> 00:29:49,960
and you just can't get over

751
00:29:49,960 --> 00:29:51,240
the hurdles,

752
00:29:51,240 --> 00:29:51,800
the obstacles,

753
00:29:51,800 --> 00:29:53,280
the darkness in your life.

754
00:29:53,280 --> 00:29:57,440
I love how John ends his gospel,

755
00:29:57,440 --> 00:29:59,760
how he resolves the story.

756
00:29:59,760 --> 00:30:00,980
He resolves his story

757
00:30:00,980 --> 00:30:01,880
with Jesus going

758
00:30:01,880 --> 00:30:03,520
to three different individuals

759
00:30:03,520 --> 00:30:06,860
who have three very real reasons

760
00:30:06,860 --> 00:30:08,380
for not wanting to believe.

761
00:30:08,380 --> 00:30:12,520
And Jesus speaks their name.

762
00:30:12,520 --> 00:30:16,620
So as we begin

763
00:30:16,620 --> 00:30:18,120
to close this morning,

764
00:30:18,120 --> 00:30:20,140
I just want to look

765
00:30:20,140 --> 00:30:20,900
at these three accounts

766
00:30:20,900 --> 00:30:22,420
and ask you to consider

767
00:30:22,420 --> 00:30:23,360
if you find yourself

768
00:30:23,360 --> 00:30:24,560
in one of these situations,

769
00:30:24,560 --> 00:30:26,320
is it possible?

770
00:30:26,320 --> 00:30:28,460
Is it possible that Jesus

771
00:30:28,460 --> 00:30:29,680
wants to speak your name

772
00:30:29,680 --> 00:30:30,200
this morning?

773
00:30:30,900 --> 00:30:31,940
Is it possible

774
00:30:31,940 --> 00:30:32,880
that the obstacles

775
00:30:32,880 --> 00:30:35,080
that you have allowed

776
00:30:35,080 --> 00:30:35,880
to keep you

777
00:30:35,880 --> 00:30:37,280
from believing in Jesus

778
00:30:37,280 --> 00:30:38,040
are obstacles

779
00:30:38,040 --> 00:30:39,440
that he has already overcome?

780
00:30:39,440 --> 00:30:43,640
In John chapter 20,

781
00:30:43,640 --> 00:30:45,300
Jesus first goes to a woman

782
00:30:45,300 --> 00:30:47,900
who is crippled

783
00:30:47,900 --> 00:30:49,360
with grief and suffering.

784
00:30:49,360 --> 00:30:50,440
Her name's Mary.

785
00:30:50,440 --> 00:30:51,480
She stood,

786
00:30:51,480 --> 00:30:52,260
we already read it,

787
00:30:52,260 --> 00:30:53,440
she stood weeping

788
00:30:53,440 --> 00:30:55,380
outside the tomb.

789
00:30:58,660 --> 00:30:59,800
She can't find him.

790
00:30:59,800 --> 00:31:00,920
She's talking to angels

791
00:31:00,920 --> 00:31:01,520
and doesn't seem

792
00:31:01,520 --> 00:31:02,920
to be that freaked out about it.

793
00:31:02,920 --> 00:31:04,540
And she turns around,

794
00:31:04,540 --> 00:31:05,180
she sees somebody

795
00:31:05,180 --> 00:31:06,760
that she thinks is a gardener

796
00:31:06,760 --> 00:31:07,560
and it's Jesus

797
00:31:07,560 --> 00:31:08,000
and he says,

798
00:31:08,000 --> 00:31:09,080
woman, why are you weeping?

799
00:31:09,080 --> 00:31:10,320
Whom are you seeking?

800
00:31:10,320 --> 00:31:11,880
Supposing him

801
00:31:11,880 --> 00:31:12,480
to be the gardener,

802
00:31:12,480 --> 00:31:12,980
she said to him,

803
00:31:12,980 --> 00:31:13,920
sir, if you've carried him away,

804
00:31:13,920 --> 00:31:15,360
tell me where you have laid him

805
00:31:15,360 --> 00:31:16,660
and I will take him away.

806
00:31:16,660 --> 00:31:17,640
And Jesus said to her,

807
00:31:17,640 --> 00:31:18,100
Mary.

808
00:31:18,100 --> 00:31:21,020
And immediately her name

809
00:31:21,020 --> 00:31:22,640
snapped her out of it.

810
00:31:22,640 --> 00:31:24,760
She no longer supposes him

811
00:31:24,760 --> 00:31:25,520
to be the gardener,

812
00:31:25,520 --> 00:31:26,000
but she says,

813
00:31:26,000 --> 00:31:26,700
Rabboni,

814
00:31:26,700 --> 00:31:27,960
my teacher, my Lord.

815
00:31:29,580 --> 00:31:30,140
And God,

816
00:31:30,140 --> 00:31:31,780
and Jesus goes out of his way

817
00:31:31,780 --> 00:31:32,640
for the first time

818
00:31:32,640 --> 00:31:33,180
in the gospel.

819
00:31:33,180 --> 00:31:34,940
He refers to God

820
00:31:34,940 --> 00:31:36,000
as my father

821
00:31:36,000 --> 00:31:37,420
and your father,

822
00:31:37,420 --> 00:31:38,720
my God

823
00:31:38,720 --> 00:31:39,620
and your God.

824
00:31:39,620 --> 00:31:40,400
New creation

825
00:31:40,400 --> 00:31:41,560
is breaking through.

826
00:31:41,560 --> 00:31:44,020
Mary is distraught.

